LFW face verification task
##########################

I compared between three models trained from scratch.

Each model is trained with ResNet18 or simple cnn architecture as a backbone
for computing the embeddings, which are later used with cosine similarity to verify
person's identity.

The first model - resnet18 + infoNCE loss is used
The second model - resnet18 + arcFace loss is used
The third model - cnn + arcFace loss is used

Dataset:
I used the following files:
matchpairsDevTrain.csv - Same-person pairs for View 1 train (~1100)
mismatchpairsDevTrain.csv - Different-person pairs for View 1 train (~1100)
matchpairsDevTest.csv - Same-person pairs for View 1 VALIDATION (~500)
mismatchpairsDevTest.csv - Different-person pairs for View 1 VALIDATION (~500)
pairs.csv - Official View 2 pairs (~6000) for final 10-fold reporting

For infoNCE model, peopleDevTrain with images >= 2 are used (need a positive pair)

Conclusions:
All models had a solid LFW-only results of about 81% mean accuracy on the 10-fold final report
This is far below the 99%+ numbers I saw in other papers that used huge external face datasets.
I did not expect much more from this setup without pretrained face weights and more identities.
